WEBVTT

00:02:27.064 --> 00:02:31.217
It also affects an instrument’s ability 
to stand out in a crowd,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:36.647
because our ears are more strongly 
attuned to some frequencies than others.

00:02:36.647 --> 00:02:40.947
This is the key to an opera singer’s 
power of projection.

00:02:40.947 --> 00:02:42.437
An operatic soprano—

00:02:42.437 --> 00:02:44.797
the highest of the four standard 
voice parts—

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.627
can produce notes 
with fundamental frequencies

00:02:47.627 --> 00:02:53.047
ranging from 250 to 1,500 vibrations 
per second.

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:55.737
Human ears are most sensitive 
to frequencies

00:02:55.737 --> 00:02:59.737
between 2,000 and 5,000 
vibrations per second.

00:02:59.737 --> 00:03:03.657
So if the singer can bring out 
the partials in this range,